let's speak now to Saudi Arabia's  ambassador to the UK as Royal Highness  Prince Khalid bin bandar al-saud who's  at the labor Party Conference in  Liverpool thank you very much for being  with us and uh first of all I wonder  tell us more about the role that Saudi  Arabia played in this release of British  prisoners and others held by Russian  proxy forces how did Saudi Arabia get  involved  uh well thank you for having me Mark  um so is Royal Highness the Crown Prince  from the very start of the conflict  offered to provide whatever help he  could to bring the conflict to an end in  March last year he spoke to both  presidents zielinski and Putin in and  offered you know any measures that Saudi  Arabia could provide  by April he had started hearing that  there was a complication in a prisoner  swap bill that was being negotiated and  the sticking point was these 10 foreign  Fighters he took it upon himself to get  involved quietly as we like to conduct  our diplomacy and used his offices to  you know  negotiate and discuss with with  President Putin on the release of the  the 10 and I'm very proud and happy to  say he managed to convince the president  and they're all back with our families  now safe and sound right so this was a  President Putin's request because a good  friend of his is also released and other  Russians was it a President Putin's  request  no not at all the discussions that the  wider discussions that were happening  with other countries and other leaders  around the world principally in Turkey  were happening concurrently his Royal  Highness got involved himself  he believed it was the right thing to do  it's a good humanitarian cause he'd had  discussions with various world leaders  who had prisoners in Russia and thought  he would see what he could do to help  okay now Crown Prince as you say got  involved  um  and the prisoners are clearly very  grateful do you think it helps to  rebuild relations with the West after  the khashoggi killing the murder of  which the Saudi government was  implicated in was that part of this  not not directly no um  I think the Crown Prince saw the  opportunity to do the right thing  nothing more nothing less and he saw  you know we conduct our diplomacy  um quite often in a quiet way we don't  always have to be seen to be doing the  right thing we just do the right thing  when we see there's an opportunity to do  so and I think this is a good example of  that it's also a good example of us  doing what we can for our friends around  the world  um our alliance with the UK goes back  100 years so there's nothing more than  that I I would I would say but it does  provide an example of where we can play  a huge role in a significant role to  help things along around the world right  I mean stability is is as important for  us as anyone else okay it also shows a  close relationship with Russia a  relationship that seems to have survived  the invasion of Ukraine does Saudi  Arabia condemn that invasion  I mean you would have seen our voting  record at the U.N we don't believe that  um issues between nations can be solved  by infringing upon territorial  sovereignty and with that applies to us  in our region as it does anywhere else  in the world  um  we would like to see the conflict  brought to an end it affects everyone in  the world not just through Energy prices  but you know the Grain and food stuff  imports from Ukraine and Russia into the  Middle East are incredibly significant  so food security is important  um but it's also important this is a  very good example of the fact that we  have the ability to talk to many people  I think shows and highlights the  importance of Saudi Arabia we can talk  to the East and the South the way that  that many others can't and I think  um that's not something to be to be  scoffed at and I think this shows uh how  important of a player is Saudi Arabia's  uh to the you know the world order well  I mean but much of the world has turned  its back on President Putin he's  considered a pariah Saudi Arabia has  invested increased investment in Russia  it's increased the oil you're buying  from Russia you're helping to prop up  oil prices with Russia should you not be  isolating uh this man who has  um you know invaded an independent  country in the way he has  um International prisoners are now free  had we  isolated Russia we wouldn't have been  able to achieve that that aim and so I  think that the families of those that  have been returned to them be very  grateful that we did manage to bridge a  gap there's always a place for someone  to bridge a gap and that's what we're  doing we have a tremendous relationship  with the West as we do with the East and  it's practical on many fronts  but it's important to keep that dialogue  going that's how we believe we engage  with the world is to keep the dialogue  going we engage with people we don't  like all the time  How concerned are you by what you're  seeing in Iran these protests by women  who are fed up with the way that they're  being treated when it comes to dress and  so forth uh does it worry you or will it  encourage you to bring more change to  Saudi Arabia  were there two elements to that question  I think we we are watching what's  happening in Iran with great concern  um Iran uh is obviously a major player  in our region and in further instability  Iran is not good for anyone I think that  they need to have a good look at the  policies that they have and what it's  doing to their people if you look at  Saudi Arabia it's part of the second  part of your question  not just the last five years the last 10  15 20 100 years you've seen a positive  development Trend in the way Saudi  Arabia is developed and I think it's a  it's an example to many of how you can  improve things and I think  not just Iran but many people can learn  from that uh that change in that  positive development and and I think  they need it there but ambassadors you  can see with the protests but Ambassador  women's rights in your country are still  heavily curtailed a male relative is  still required to give permission for a  woman to get married to to start certain  sorts of businesses there's still  restrictions on a women's dress code in  several areas of Saudi Arabia  the inlook one can pick a snapshot of  the development of a country and use  that as the defining character you know  period of time but if you look at the  where we've gone where we've come from  and the change that's happened in the  particularly the last five years is  dramatic 45 percent of Enterprises new  Enterprise in Saudi are run by women uh  37 of our labor force is now women and  that's gone up 300 in four years  um the majority of the guardianship  guardianship system has been uh  eliminated and so right you can't just  take a picture and say this is where you  are you have to look at where we're  going and where we've been yeah I don't  know I do I do yeah we're looking good  there has been change but many women's  rights activists are still  obviously in prison look we're running  out of time but I just want to end  finally with why the Crown Prince didn't  go to the Queen's funeral is this a  result of these still  difficult relations because of what  happened to khashoggi and  you know the Saudi government's role in  that  no not so we had you know the the the  funeral was obviously something that  happened unexpectedly and last minute  and we couldn't manage to figure out  some of the details involved in in the  uh the trip uh you know the movement of  someone  it was it can do a head of state is not  easy  and there's nothing more to it than that  and just there's certainly no problems  between travel and hopefully we'll have  a trip soon and just finally though do  you accept the damage that has been done  to the relationship with this country  and other Western countries by the  murder of khashoggi  happen in Istanbul sustained on the  relationship the  reputation of Saudi not just as a  government but as a country and its  people and I wish it had never happened  but we've we've done what we can to stop  it from happening again and I think like  I said it's positive developments in  Saudi and I think that's that's what we  need to focus on  all right Ambassador listen I appreciate  your time thanks for coming on the  program  thank you for having me

